---
description: Flutter Result and Failure error handling
globs: flutter_app/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the sealed Result<T> pattern:
- Success<T>
- FailureResult<T>

Use the existing sealed Failure hierarchy defined in:
packages/core/lib/src/domain/

Never introduce:
- dartz
- Either
- another competing Result pattern

Repositories must never expose DioException or raw Dio Response objects.

Map infrastructure/network errors to the appropriate Failure inside the
repository implementation.

Failures must carry a FailureCode enum rather than hardcoded English strings.

Localized display messages for failures must be resolved in the presentation
layer through intl/ARB files.
